{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"P999000ed"},"owner_reference":"#3978","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"P999000ed\",\"feature\":\"primary-quota-403-retryable\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Classify GitHub primary-quota rate-limit refusals as retryable with a bounded reset-derived retry_after on every REST and GraphQL path; align probe_backend_status with the same classifier (A); bound PyGithub's in-transport primary-limit wait (B); populate ViewItemResult.number (C); remove dead ViewItemResultCompact; keep permission-denied 403s, GraphQL refusals and secondary limits unchanged.\",\"context\":\"# Plan context: #3978 primary-quota 403 retryable\\n\\nInputs every task reads itself: `artifact_read(item_id=3978, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")` (spec, sections cited per task as 'spec \\u00a7N'), `artifact_read(item_id=3978, artifact_type=\\\"feature-context\\\")`, and `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3978\\\", summary=False, sections=[\\\"Acceptance Criteria\\\"])` (12 ACs).\\n\\n## Test runner (verified 2026-09-28)\\nRun from the repo root: `uv run --locked --script plugins/development-harness/run_pytests.py <paths relative to plugin root> -q`. A bare `uv run pytest` from the repo root fails on this plugin's conftest import (`tests.network_blocked`). Loopback sockets are allowed by the plugin conftest network guard; all other network is blocked.\\n\\n## Planning decisions (auto mode)\\n- D1 reset-delay boundary: `rate_limit_reset_delay_seconds` returns `min((reset - now) + 1.0, 3900.0)`, and returns `None` when that value is <= 0, or when the header is absent, empty, non-numeric or non-finite. Consequence: reset == now gives 1.0; reset 1s or more in the past gives None. This settles the spec \\u00a76 'confirm exact boundary' note and the spec \\u00a72 Q1 / \\u00a74.1 wording mismatch.\\n- D2 (orchestrator): `requests.exceptions.RetryError` as retryable (spec \\u00a73.3) is its own task (T2) so review can judge it separately.\\n- D3 (orchestrator): a test pins PyGithub `GithubRetry().secondary_rate_wait == 60` and urllib3 `Retry.DEFAULT_BACKOFF_MAX == 120` as installed, and that the \\u00a79 threshold stays above both (T5). Observed values on 2026-09-28: 60 and 120.\\n- D4 (orchestrator): delete dead `ViewItemResultCompact` only after a search proves no reference (T7). This supersedes spec \\u00a77's Non-Goal on that class.\\n- D5 (orchestrator): Issue C is reproduce-first (T6 step 1 records failing output).\\n- D6: tests are written before or alongside each fix (TDD). Every task names its exact verification command.\\n\\n## Planning assumptions (unknown-frontier closures)\\n- U1 (GraphQL delay path in or out of scope): closed by spec \\u00a74.2a and AC9. In scope, T3.\\n- U2 (live primary-limit responses carry `x-ratelimit-reset` behind proxies): not verifiable offline, and running the live e2e lane locally against the production backlog is forbidden (AGENTS.md). Assumption: PyGithub passes response headers through unmodified (spec \\u00a73.2, Requester.createException). When the header is missing, the fix falls back to `retry_after=None` plus the sync engine's fixed 30/120s floor (spec Q1). No task. Residual risk is recorded for TN.\\n\\n## File ownership (same-file conflicts serialized by dependencies)\\n- sync_state.py: T1 then T2. tests/test_sync_state_classify.py: T1 then T2.\\n- gh_client.py: T3 only (GraphQL fallback and probe_backend_status merged).\\n- github_client.py and backlog_core/tests/test_github_client.py: T4 only. T5 writes a new file.\\n- parsing.py: T6. models.py: T7. backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md: T8.\\n- sync_engine.py, server.py and backends/github_backend.py are verify-only (T9). No task edits them.\\n\\n## Sync checkpoints\\n- SC1 (after T1): the classifier and delay helper are green, AC1-AC4 tests pass, and AC5-AC7 suites pass unmodified. Gates T2, T3 and T4.\\n- SC2 (after T2-T7): every structured-criterion suite passes, and `git diff` shows no edits to the verify-only files. Gates T8 and T9. Reflect: do the classifier (T1/T2), probe_backend_status (T3) and bounded retry (T4) agree on one rate-limit definition?\\n- SC3 (TN): baseline-versus-final comparison of the structured criteria.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3978\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T0\",\"title\":\"T0: Capture baseline state\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"t0-baseline-capture\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-testing\"],\"created\":\"2026-09-28T10:10:08.407349+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\",\"is_bookend\":true,\"bookend_type\":\"t0-baseline\"}],\"source_path\":null,\"state\":\"drafting\",\"acceptance_criteria_structured\":[{\"criterion_id\":\"AC-SUITES\",\"description\":\"Every touched or adjacent suite passes, including the new tests (item ACs 1-12). Baseline fails because new tests and the new file do not exist yet.\",\"check_command\":\"uv run --locked --script plugins/development-harness/run_pytests.py tests/test_retryable_classification.py backlog_core/tests/test_rate_limit_retry_after.py tests/test_sync_state_secondary_rate_limit.py backlog_core/tests/test_startup_sync.py tests/test_sync_state_graphql_refusal.py tests/test_sync_state_classify.py backlog_core/tests/test_graphql_rate_limit_detection.py tests/test_backend_status.py backlog_core/tests/test_github_client.py backlog_core/tests/test_upstream_retry_defaults.py tests/test_backlog_core_parsing.py backlog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py -q\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC-LINT\",\"description\":\"ruff lint and format are clean for backlog_core (clean at baseline, 2026-09-28).\",\"check_command\":\"uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/backlo